# Logging (structured, useful)

Use `[vtw]` structured logs for app API work and Edge Functions. Full catalog: `docs/LOGGING_COMBINED.md`.

## Required
- Wrap client API/backend ops with `withApiLog(scope, fields, fn)` (`src/lib/with-api-log.ts`).
- Edge: `edgeLog(level, scope, fields)` from `supabase/functions/_shared/log.ts`.
- Failures must include **`code`** (stable machine id) and **`reason`** (real cause — provider/DB/validation message). No generic-only `"Something went wrong"` in logs.
- Prefer `ApiError(code, reason)` for app-thrown failures (`src/lib/api-error.ts`).
- UI copy uses `errorMessageForUi` / `authErrorMessage` (the reason).

## Forbidden in logs
Audio, transcripts, prompts, passwords, OTP, tokens, auth headers, signed URLs, API keys.

## Format
Pretty JSON block (2-space indent), prefixed with `[vtw]`:
```
[vtw]
{
  "ts": "...",
  "src": "app|edge",
  "level": "...",
  "scope": "...",
  "event": "...",
  "code?": "...",
  "reason?": "..."
}
```
